From 7cd5d278c0518f6d02bdf430ee79e296193c8e14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 5656565566 <contact@home56.top>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:34:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] uts: Add host-managed namespace kernel identity

Add an opt-in UTS namespace extension for container runtimes that need a
consistent kernel identity without modifying libc or replacing syscall
handlers. A host administrator configures release/version through a UTS
namespace FD. The initial UTS is immutable, successful configuration
seals both fields, and descendant UTS namespaces inherit the same
identity family.

Require initial user/PID namespace credentials and CAP_SYS_ADMIN for
SET. Restrict GET and setns across identity families to the same
administrators, including when a guest holds an otherwise usable
namespace FD. Preserve standard hostname/domainname handling and
architecture/personality ABI.

Use the configured strings for uname and existing sysctls. Remove
embedded host build identity from the configured namespace's proc
version banner, clear old bytes in uname arrays, and derive UNAME26
output from the instance release. Unconfigured namespaces retain their
existing identity.

Document the fixed native/compat ioctl ABI and add a focused nsfs
selftest for validation, sealing, inherited views and denied escape
paths. The test accepts an optional compat executable for raw AArch32
validation on arm64.
